    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 48 tests pass, including the new `Cp35Tests` (soft-match flagging) and the existing `Cp10Tests` (hard-duplicate rejection). **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe soft-match \"possible duplicate\" flag needed to be **computed at create time, persisted, and returned on GET** (mirroring how the existing `namesakeCount` / `bulkSignupWarning` fields work), since the test creates the owner then reads the fields back on a separate `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after the existing hard-duplicate check (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`) passes, a new `assignPossibleDuplicate(owner)` runs. It scans existing owners for one that shares the new owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive, consistent with the namesake rule) and exact `postcode` but has a **different** normalized telephone. If found, it sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = <matching id>` (lowest id when several match, for determinism); otherwise `possibleDuplicate = false`. An owner with no postcode has nothing to match on and is never flagged.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) persistent columns with accessors.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct auto-maps them by name (no mapper change needed).\n\n4. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb used by tests, plus h2, mysql, postgres for consistency).\n\nThe change is additive and left the hard-duplicate (409) behaviour untouched \u2014 the soft-match only runs on owners that are *not* hard duplicates, exactly as the spec requires.",
